# The station: one deck, a hub, two airlocks and a window band all the way
# round. Built by `go run ./tools/mapgen -map station`; this file is the level,
# map.bin and map.json are what it compiles to.
#
# The whole thing is described in the station's own frame, which is the only
# frame there is: the blocks never move and gravity inside is the ordinary -Y,
# so walking and jumping on the deck are the ordinary ones. The sky is what
# turns - see `spin` - which is the same relative motion either way, through a
# window or from outside the hull.

size 96 24 96

# Space: no horizon for the cubemap to fade into, nothing close enough to fog,
# and enough ambient that the outside of the hull is not a silhouette.
sky full
spin 6
fog 200 900
ambient 0.25 0.30 0.45 0.10
ceiling 4 5 10
floor 4 5 10
music maintenance

# Inside this cylinder there is air, a floor and gravity; outside it there is
# the suit. It is the hull and nothing else decides it - which is why an
# airlock chamber, which sticks out past the hull, is already vacuum by the
# time you are standing in it.
pressure 48 48 26 10 15

# --------------------------------------------------------------- materials ---
# Three textures a block: the four sides, the top, the underside.
block deck 21 22 20
block roof 21 28 20
block hull 28 28 28
block hub 39 39 39
block lock 20 22 20
# The one texture here the atlas marks as glowing (see the emIS chunk): a lit
# strip under the windows, which is the deck's own light indoors and the line
# that makes the hull read as turning from outside.
block trim 27 22 20

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- decks ---
# One deck: a floor slab, a ceiling slab, and three voxels of room between them
# (y 11, 12, 13). Everything below stands on those numbers.
cyl deck 48 48 26 10 10
cyl roof 48 48 26 14 14

# The outer wall, in two courses with nothing between them: a window band the
# whole way round at y=12. The sill is a voxel above the floor, which is higher
# than a jump, so it is a window rather than a way out.
tube trim 48 48 26 25 11 11
tube hull 48 48 26 25 13 13

# ...and the glass in it. A pane is see-through to look at and wall to walk
# into, so the band is a window rather than a way out or a way in.
glass 48 48 26 25 12

# The hub in the middle, so the deck is a ring corridor rather than a field.
# Two doorways into it, east and west.
tube hub 48 48 8 7 11 13
clear 40 11 47 41 13 49
clear 55 11 47 56 13 49

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- airlocks ---
# Each is a box hanging off the hull with a one-voxel passage bored through it,
# an inner door in the hull course and an outer door at the far end. The mouth
# past the outer door is open to space.
#
# The passage is two voxels tall because that is what a slide door needs: the
# leaf is one voxel and it opens by rising one. The voxel above each door is
# filled back in afterwards, so a shut door is a shut doorway rather than one
# with a slot of sky over it, and an open one has slid up inside the lintel.
fill lock 46 10 16 50 14 23
clear 48 11 16 48 12 24
fill lock 48 12 23 48 12 23
fill lock 48 12 18 48 12 18
entity SlideDoor mesh=door_slide at=48.5,11,23.5
entity SlideDoor mesh=door_slide at=48.5,11,18.5

fill lock 46 10 73 50 14 80
clear 48 11 72 48 12 80
fill lock 48 12 73 48 12 73
fill lock 48 12 78 48 12 78
entity SlideDoor mesh=door_slide at=48.5,11,73.5
entity SlideDoor mesh=door_slide at=48.5,11,78.5

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ lights ---
# Baked, so the deck can have as many as it likes: eight round the ring, one in
# the hub, one in each airlock.
light 64.5 13.5 48.5 color=1,0.90,0.75 power=6 baked
light 59.8 13.5 59.8 color=1,0.90,0.75 power=6 baked
light 48.5 13.5 64.5 color=1,0.90,0.75 power=6 baked
light 37.2 13.5 59.8 color=1,0.90,0.75 power=6 baked
light 32.5 13.5 48.5 color=1,0.90,0.75 power=6 baked
light 37.2 13.5 37.2 color=1,0.90,0.75 power=6 baked
light 48.5 13.5 32.5 color=1,0.90,0.75 power=6 baked
light 59.8 13.5 37.2 color=1,0.90,0.75 power=6 baked
light 48.5 13.5 48.5 color=1,0.90,0.75 power=6 baked
light 48.5 11.5 20.5 color=0.7,0.85,1 power=6 baked
light 48.5 11.5 76.5 color=0.7,0.85,1 power=6 baked

# Two lamps that cast a real shadow, one over each inner door, so the airlock
# reads as a threshold rather than a hole.
light 48.5 13.8 24.5 color=0.75,0.85,1 power=7 pitch=90 angle=110 reach=9
light 48.5 13.8 71.5 color=0.75,0.85,1 power=7 pitch=90 angle=110 reach=9

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- start ---
# On the deck, in the ring corridor, facing the north airlock.
spawn 48.5 11 28.5 dir=0,-1
